WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.760
Make it: whipped shea butter, oils, balms and testing.

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.660
This is the video for module 2 of Organic Skincare and Hair Products.

3
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.730
Good whipped butter is light, smooth and holds its shape in the jar.

4
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:21.310
Poor whipped butter is gritty, collapses into a greasy puddle, or smells stale. The difference is method.

5
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:30.650
Write every formula in percentages, then convert to grams, so a 200 g batch and a 2 kg batch come out the same.

6
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.370
And test what you make, properly, before anyone pays for it.

7
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:47.180
Safety first. Melt over a pot of gently simmering water, called a double boiler. Keep the heat low. Shea should never smoke or boil, and you never leave the pot.

8
00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:52.270
Melted oils can cause serious burns, so keep children away.

9
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.780
Keep a lid nearby. If oil ever catches fire, cover the pan. Never pour water on burning oil.

10
00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:11.520
A reliable starting formula is about 70% shea butter and 30% liquid oil. For a 500 g batch, that is 350 g of shea.

11
00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:20.430
Melt the shea and coconut oil until there are no solid bits at all, then keep it melted for about 10 more minutes, stirring.

12
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:30.830
Off the heat, add the olive oil. Cool quickly in a bowl of cold water with ice, stirring, until the middle is like soft custard or thick pap.

13
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.110
Add essential oil now, when it is cool, so less scent evaporates.

14
00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.520
Whip with a hand mixer for 5 to 10 minutes, until pale and light.

15
00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.380
Fill clean, dry jars and label with batch number and date.

16
00:01:47.630 --> 00:02:00.300
Slow cooling causes grainy butter. Bisi in Lagos cooled her first batch slowly overnight, and customers said it felt sandy. She remelted, cooled it fast and whipped again, and it was smooth.

17
00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:19.940
Decide what the oil is for before choosing oils. A scalp oil is massaged in a few times a week, so it is light and low in essential oil. Chioma's 100 g scalp oil has 50 g light coconut oil, 29 g olive, 20 g castor, and 1 g lavender.

18
00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:26.610
A sealing oil for lengths and ends can be richer, with castor up to about 40%.

19
00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.600
Her label promises softening, not growth.

20
00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:42.780
A balm is oil made solid with wax. About 20% wax gives a firm balm. For 100 g, weigh 20 g beeswax, 30 g shea and 50 g olive oil.

21
00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:50.000
Melt over a double boiler on low heat. Beeswax takes longer than shea. Stir until clear.

22
00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:59.660
Dip a cold spoon in, let it set for a minute, and press. Too hard, add a little oil. Too soft, add a little wax. Record the change.

23
00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:09.740
Stir in essential oil at a low level. On lips, avoid cinnamon, clove and citrus oils. Pour into dry tins and leave to set.

24
00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:18.880
The American Academy of Dermatology advises a simple test. Give each tester a labelled sample and the instructions.

25
00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:25.960
Apply the normal amount on the inner arm or elbow bend, twice a day for 7 to 10 days.

26
00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:31.200
If redness, itching or swelling appears, she stops and tells you.

27
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:36.970
Only after a clear test should she use it on the face, scalp or whole body.

28
00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:44.960
If someone reacts, tell her to wash it off and see a health worker if it is severe. Do not suggest home remedies.

29
00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:51.930
Test hair products for about four weeks, with at least five testers whose hair is different from yours.

30
00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:58.340
Ask how it felt, how the smell was, any itching or flaking, and whether they would buy it.

31
00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:11.600
Halima's scalp oil had 25% castor. Four of six testers said it felt heavy. She changed only one thing, castor down to 15%, and five of six then liked it.

32
00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:21.150
To remember. Low heat, and never leave the pot. Melt fully, hold, then cool fast. Decide the job before you choose the oils.

33
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:26.620
Test on the inner arm for 7 to 10 days, and change only one thing between rounds.

34
00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:36.770
Your turn. Make a 200 g whipped butter and check it after two weeks. Write and make a 100 g hair oil, and a 50 g balm.

35
00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.960
Then run a trial with at least five testers and keep every form.

36
00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.250
Continue with the lessons below.
